+- Drama speech accepts dialogue tags `<|speaker:0|>` through `<|speaker:15|>` in whole and streamed HTTP requests and catalog reference transcripts. Untagged text still uses speaker 0, and catalogs still allow at most four reference passages. See [dialogue speakers](docs/drama-http-voices.md#dialogue-speakers).
+
 - Drama speech requests accept `temperature`, `top_p`, `top_k` (1 through 64) and exact unsigned 64-bit `seed` values. Whole replies, streams, catalog voices and redraws retain the requested settings; omitted or null fields keep the existing defaults. Explicit seeds advance by the attempt number for redraws. See [speech sampling](docs/speech-sampling.md).
 
 - Combined silence onset and mid settings append their clauses to the base startup sentence in onset-then-mid order; the mid clause includes its required voiced minimum.
